    "summary": "No new step this turn: roughly five minutes of the run's total budget remain, every question in the record is locally answered or explicitly bounded, there are no open necessary gaps, and I am not spending the remaining time on a marginal item or a duplicate revision. The returned path is the last accepted draft, unchanged, so the controller records no_change rather than a new revision.\n\nFor the offline reviewer, the run ends with this state, all of it backed by retained receipts or by cited source:\n\nConfirmed defects. (1) A leadership-transfer order is received without any authority binding: `TimeoutNow` carries no term, the receiver clears the leader and enters Candidate while setting the leadership-transfer flag, which suppresses pre-vote and the known-leader vote rejection — one order from a non-member claimed sender deposed a serving leader, with a stale-term RequestVote control unchanged (receipt 8248101f2e7e47ecae3104f94cd0357b). (2) `GetConfiguration().Index()` is constant zero, and the `prevIndex` guard only fires for non-zero values, so a membership change guarded with the value the API returned is applied after an intervening change while the genuine-index control is rejected (receipt 11917033a9654d628e6d1452583ddd8e). (3) A node recovered through InstallSnapshot keeps its log store index below the snapshot index, making `shouldSnapshot`'s unsigned delta permanently true: it rewrites an identical full-state snapshot every SnapshotInterval while idle (two executions, 15 and 13 distinct snapshot IDs at one index, against 1 for the leader control).\n\nConditional finding. A below-protocol-2 leader writes membership changes in the deprecated voter-only peer format, and the constructor restores versioned configurations regardless of protocol version, so a rollback-style deployment can silently drop non-voting members; quorum cannot be lost and the library neither prevents nor warns about the rollback.\n\nNegative results retained with their boundaries: snapshot recency is enforced only against the term (and executes a control-backed run with no applied-index regression), a stranded leader's `VerifyLeader` completes with an error in the order of the leader lease, `ReloadConfig` rejects a constructor-invalid merged configuration without changing anything, configuration propagation converged in 25 of 25 rounds with no node publishing stale membership while holding the entry, pipelined replication's optimistic cursor never becomes acknowledged state, the heartbeat fast path's mutations are lock-protected, and the log-store, barrier, progress-accessor, shutdown, observation and existing-state contracts are documented with their explicit limits. Unresolved boundaries — the un-reproduced local failure of the captured upgrade test, and the heartbeat fast path being unexecutable without a network namespace — are recorded as such rather than smoothed over."
